here we go again Sony have revealed the  six No the eight free games we'll be  receiving as part of PS plus for the  month of August 2018 and oh my goodness  it's a damn good month as always these  games will be available from around  midday on the first Tuesday of the month  this time around that's the seventh of  August let's start with the offerings on  ps4 and first up is the exceptional  Mafia 3 it's an open-world crime fest  set back in the 1960s in a reimagining  of new orleans known as new bordeaux  first released in October 2016 mafia 3  follows Lincoln Clay as he returns from  the Vietnam War the story and acting are  fantastic packed with political tension  and top-notch action seems all  complemented by great visuals and  impressive sound design mechanically  though this isn't up to the same  standards as say GTA 5 and feels  repetitive if you don't commit to the  narrative the reviews reflected this  feeling with scores ranging from as low  as two out of five to seven out of ten  from your friends over at IGN you're  gonna have to download this one and see  which of the review scores you agree  with next up we have a slice of survival  horror to get your teeth into this is  dead by daylight but it's not the  standard version it's the special  edition complete with additional maps  killers and survivors if you're new to  asymmetric multiplayer here's a  breakdown one player begins the game as  the killer most of which are based on  movie murderers like Michael Myers they  are tasked with eliminating everyone in  the game all those other people must  survive and attempt to escape by using  the right tools and working together  there's a lot of blood in this one so  it's not for the squeamish ps+ gives us  two additional games this month with the  first being the play link titled  knowledge is power  your task is to get your mate around and  use your phones  answering questions and dragging  yourself to victory that's not the end  though there's also a psvr title here  too here they lie described as a dark  psychological horror I'm not sure how I  feel about this one but I'm tempted to  make a follow-up let's play video here  they light asks you with uncovering a  mystery buried in your nightmares come  on whose man are woman enough to try  this one over on the ps3 is serious Sam  BFP it's a throwback to the golden  generation of first-person shooters it's  a balls-to-the-wall rampage through so  many different types of weapons you'll  definitely get used to the sight of  blood with Serious Sam released almost  seven years ago it hasn't aged  fantastically well but it's a great nod  to the 90s next on the ps3 is bound by  flame a fantasy themed action RPG from  back in 2014  your character is possessed by a demon  sounds lovely doesn't it all the typical  RPG elements are here designing your own  characters crafting weapons and  upgrading passive and active abilities  game informer love this one and gave it  8 out of 10 over on the Vita is Space  Hulk if you're a fan of Warhammer 40k  you'll probably already know about Space  Hulk but if not this is a turn-based  strategy game officially licensed by  Games Workshop it takes its rules from  the classic board game with added  cinematics to spice up the narrative  definitely one for the enthusiasts its  average 6 point 5 out of 10 in reviews  and finally draw slasher this one is  telefon draw slasher uses the  touchscreen to both move your character  and attack using gestures it doesn't  take itself seriously and allows you to  cut monkeys in half think of it like a  gruesome fruit ninja definitely worth  the download so there we have it eight  games to get your teeth into on top of  this are the PlayStation exclusive skin  and back bling that are still available  in fortnight battle royale and a few  goodies for fallout shelter and h1z1 -  so what's the month's theme blood and  violence I can't wait to try dead by  daylight and maybe the psvr horror title  if I can pluck up the courage what are  you grabbing I'd love to know your  thoughts throw them down in the comments  below  I'm Adam from Playstation grenade it's  been a pleasure I'll see you next time  [Music]
 

